{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/pulls/8521","id":5007182932,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAAfumM8AAAABKnOMVA","html_url":"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/pull/8521","diff_url":"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/pull/8521.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/pull/8521.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/8521","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/pulls/8521/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/pulls/8521/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/issues/8521/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mitmproxy/mitmproxy/statuses/2eaf36ed37eddd28a4026b71ebab1b55cd7123df","number":8521,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Preserve caller value lists in MultiDict.set_all","user":{"login":"hakarrr","id":191973953,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3FKQQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191973953?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakarrr","html_url":"https://github.com/hakarrr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakarrr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakarrr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakarrr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakarrr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakarrr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakarrr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakarrr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakarrr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hakarrr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"#### Description\n\n`MultiDict.set_all()` consumes its caller's list with `pop(0)`. This also affects `MultiDictView`, including `Request.query` and request cookies.\n\nFor example, an addon applying the same query values to two flows silently drops the parameter from the second flow:\n\n```python\nvalues = [\"one\", \"two\"]\nfirst.query.set_all(\"id\", values)\nsecond.query.set_all(\"id\", values)\n```\n\nThe first call empties `values`, so the second call removes `id` rather than assigning it. Copy the list before consuming it. Existing field order, duplicate-key handling, capitalization and removal behavior stay unchanged. This does not change `Headers.set_all()`, which already materializes its own list.\n\nTests cover empty, single and multiple replacement values against absent, single and case-insensitive duplicate keys, plus reuse through two real `Request.query` views while preserving an unrelated parameter. Seven new cases fail on unchanged base `9125647`; all ten pass with the fix.\n\nValidation in a separate current-main tree, without the changes from #8518 or #8520:\n\n- 267 coretype, HTTP helper and HTTP model tests pass.\n- Broader Python run excluding the tools directory: 1877 passed, 1 skipped, one failure creating a TUN device. The same TUN test fails against unchanged source in this environment.\n- Repository-wide Ruff checks pass; changed Python files are formatted.\n- Mypy: no issues in 253 source files.\n\nNo full tools test suite, live proxy session or Windows/macOS run was performed.\n\n#### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have updated tests where applicable.\n- [x] I have added an entry to the CHANGELOG.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T17:52:29Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T19:27:28Z","closed_at":"2026-10-25T18:54:07Z","merged_at":"2026-10-25T18:54:07Z","merge_commit_sha":"3f81168ac7937930f5d10c0fdf8399088254a8fd","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"hakarrr:fix/preserve-multidict-input-values","ref":"fix/preserve-multidict-input-values","rep